flowchart TD
    box_0(["Start"])
    box_1["Record the orientation error type (rotation angle,<br/>flipped, lateral offset) and the indexing table<br/>position at which the error was detected. Collect<br/>three mis oriented parts for reference."]
    box_2{"Is the orientation error occurring on parts from all<br/>indexing table positions or only from specific<br/>positions?"}
    box_3["Complete the following checks: 1. Inspect the<br/>affected nest position for contamination or damage.<br/>2. Check whether the ejector pin height at that<br/>position matches the others."]
    box_4["Clean the affected nest position and verify ejector<br/>pin height. rerun a single position test cycle to<br/>confirm the fix."]
    box_5{"Is the part feed orientation from the supply<br/>conveyor correct?"}
    box_6["Check the supply conveyor exit orientation by<br/>running a slow jog cycle and observing the part<br/>orientation as it exits the conveyor onto the<br/>indexing table."]
    box_7["Adjust the conveyor exit guide or the part<br/>singulation geometry to ensure parts arrive in the<br/>correct orientation. rerun the orientation check."]
    box_8{"Is the reorientation mechanism completing a full<br/>rotation cycle to the correct angle?"}
    box_9["Jog the reorientation mechanism through one full<br/>cycle and verify the rotation angle against the<br/>specification using a protractor or the encoder<br/>readout on the operator control interface."]
    box_10["Reteach the reorientation mechanism rotation<br/>setpoint to the correct angle. Verify with five<br/>consecutive test cycles before resuming production."]
    box_11{"Is the vision system detecting part orientation<br/>correctly when tested with known good reference<br/>parts?"}
    box_12["Test the vision system by manually placing three<br/>known good correctly oriented parts in the<br/>inspection position and checking that all three are<br/>accepted without orientation errors."]
    box_13["Complete the following steps: 1. Load the<br/>orientation calibration target into the<br/>reorientation unit fixture. 2. Run the orientation<br/>detection calibration routine from the vision system<br/>menu. 3. Capture the required number of target<br/>images at different angular positions."]
    box_14{"Is the orientation error rate within the acceptable<br/>limit after corrections?"}
    box_15["Escalate to the maintenance team: systematic<br/>orientation errors persist after all standard<br/>corrective actions have been applied."]
    box_16["Record all corrective actions and the confirmed root<br/>cause in the quality log. Notify quality assurance<br/>team."]
    box_17["Run 20 part production verification cycle at full<br/>speed, log orientation result for every part."]
    box_18[/"Refer to the orientation verification acceptance<br/>criteria."/]
    box_19{"All 20 verification parts correctly oriented, zero<br/>orientation faults?"}
    box_20(["End, Escalate: orientation fault recurring in<br/>verification run, systematic mechanism fault"])
    box_21["Check production tracking system for any mis<br/>oriented parts released to downstream assembly<br/>during fault window."]
    box_22(["End, Procedure complete. quality assurance notified,<br/>production resumed."])

